00:14:08,419 --> 00:14:12,020
possession of any of them, there lies a rough quadrilateral with its corners of

225
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:16,939
Tangier brotherville Darwin and Hong Kong, containing within it about a fifth

226
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:18,740
of the population of the earth.

227
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:22,400
It is for the possession of these thickly- populated regions, and of the

228
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:26,119
northern ice cap that the three powers are constantly struggling.

229
00:14:26,119 --> 00:14:30,740
In practice no one power ever controls the whole of the disputed area. Portions

230
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:34,520
of it are constantly changing hands, and it is the chance of seizing this or that

231
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:39,619
fragment by a sudden stroke of treachery that dictates the endless changes of alignment.

232
00:14:39,619 --> 00:14:43,759
All of the disputed territories contain valuable minerals, and some of them yield

233
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:48,137
important vegetable products such as rubber which in colder climates it is

234
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:51,979
necessary to synthesize by comparatively expensive methods.

235
00:14:51,979 --> 00:14:55,637
But above all they contain a bottomless reserve of cheap labor

236
00:14:55,637 --> 00:14:59,297
Whichever power controls equatorial Africa, or the countries of the Middle

237
00:14:59,297 --> 00:15:04,520
East, or Southern India, or the Indonesian Archipelago, disposes also of the bodies

238
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:08,540
of scores of hundreds of millions of yield paid and hard-working coulies

239
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:12,979
The inhabitants of these areas, reduced more or less openly to the status of

240
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:17,360
slaves passed continually from conqueror to conqueror, and are expended like so

241
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:21,259
much coal or oil in the race to turn out more armaments, to capture more territory,

242
00:15:21,259 --> 00:15:26,000
to control more labor power, to turn out more armaments, to capture more territory,

243
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,860
and so on indefinitely.

244
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:32,957
It should be noted that the fighting never really moves beyond the edges of the disputed areas.

245
00:15:32,957 --> 00:15:36,619
The frontiers of Eurasia flow back and forth between the basin of the Congo and

246
00:15:36,619 --> 00:15:40,400
the northern shore of the Mediterranean; the islands of the Indian Ocean under

247
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:45,137
the Pacific are constantly being captured and recaptured by Oceania or by East Asia

248
00:15:45,137 --> 00:15:49,340
in Mongolia the dividing line between Eurasia and East Asia is never stable;

249
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:53,540
round of the Pole all three powers lay claim to enormous territories which in

250
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:57,080
fact are largely uninhabited and unexplored: but the balance of power

251
00:15:57,080 --> 00:16:00,797
always remains roughly even, and the territory which forms the heartland of

252
00:16:00,797 --> 00:16:04,759
each super State always remains inviolate. Moreover, the labor of the

253
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:07,878
exploited peoples around the Equator is not really necessary to the world's

254
00:16:07,878 --> 00:16:11,779
economy. They had nothing to the wealth of the world, since whatever they produce

255
00:16:11,779 --> 00:16:15,439
is used for purposes of war, and the object of waging a war is always to be

256
00:16:15,439 --> 00:16:18,080
in a better position in which to wage another war.

257
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:23,119
By their labor the slave populations allow the tempo of continuous warfare to be speeded up.

258
00:16:23,119 --> 00:16:26,957
But if they did not exist, the structure of world society, and the process by

259
00:16:26,957 --> 00:16:31,457
which it maintains itself, would not be essentially different.

260
00:16:31,457 --> 00:16:34,939
The primary aim of modern warfare (in accordance with the principles of

261
00:16:34,939 --> 00:16:38,659
doublethink, this aim is simultaneously recognized and not recognized by the

262
00:16:38,659 --> 00:16:42,319
directing brains of the Inner Party) is to use up the products of the machine

263
00:16:42,319 --> 00:16:45,500
without raising the general standard of living.

264
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,919
Ever since the end of the 19th century, the problem of what to do with the

265
00:16:48,919 --> 00:16:52,700
surplus of consumption goods has been latent in industrial society.

266
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:56,599
At present, when few human beings even have enough to eat, this problem is

267
00:16:56,599 --> 00:17:00,979
obviously not urgent, and it might not have become so, even if no artificial

268
00:17:00,979 --> 00:17:03,797
processes of destruction had been at work.

269
00:17:03,797 --> 00:17:07,580
The world of today is a bare, hungry, dilapidated place compared with the

270
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:11,659
world that existed before 1914,. and still more so if compared with the

271
00:17:11,659 --> 00:17:15,439
imaginary future to which the people of that period looked forward.

272
00:17:15,439 --> 00:17:20,080
In the early 20th century, the vision of a future society unbelievably rich,

273
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:24,860
leisured, orderly and efficient— —a glittering antiseptic world of glass and

274
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:30,200
steel and Snow White concrete— —was part of the consciousness of nearly every literate person.

275
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:34,159
Science and technology were developing at a prodigious speed, and it seemed

276
00:17:34,159 --> 00:17:36,919
natural to assume that they would go on developing.

277
00:17:36,919 --> 00:17:40,939
This failed to happen, partly because of the impoverishment caused by a long

278
00:17:40,939 --> 00:17:44,779
series of wars and revolutions, partly because scientific and technical

279
00:17:44,779 --> 00:17:48,979
progress depended on the empirical habit of thought, which could not survive in a

280
00:17:48,979 --> 00:17:51,137
strictly regimented society.

281
00:17:51,137 --> 00:17:55,400
As a whole the world is more primitive today than it was 50 years ago. Certain

282
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:59,360
backward areas have advanced, and various devices, always in some way connected

283
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:03,378
with warfare and police espionage, have been developed, but experiment and

284
00:18:03,378 --> 00:18:07,878
invention have largely stopped, and the ravages of the atomic war of the 1950s

285
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:10,040
have never been fully repaired.

286
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:14,297
Nevertheless the dangers inherent in the machine are still there. From the moment

287
00:18:14,297 --> 00:18:17,297
when the machine first made its appearance it was clear to all thinking

288
00:18:17,297 --> 00:18:21,319
people that the need for human drudgery, and therefore to a great extent for

289
00:18:21,319 --> 00:18:26,000
human inequality, had disappeared. If the machine were used deliberately for that

290
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:30,860
end, hunger, overwork, dirt, illiteracy and disease could be eliminated within a few

291
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,240
generations.

292
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:36,020
And in fact, without being used for any such purpose, but by a sort of automatic

293
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:40,700
process— —by producing wealth which it was sometimes impossible not to distribute—

294
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:43,759
—the machine did raise the living standards of the average human being

295
00:18:43,759 --> 00:18:47,900
very greatly over a period of about 50 years at the end of the 19th and the

296
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,840
beginning of the 20th centuries.

297
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:54,259
But it was also clear that an all-round increase in wealth threatened the

298
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:59,957
destruction— —indeed, in some sense was the destruction— —of a hierarchical society.

299
00:18:59,957 --> 00:19:04,099
In a world in which everyone worked short hours, had enough to eat, lived in a

300
00:19:04,099 --> 00:19:08,957
house with a bathroom and a refrigerator, and possessed a motor car or even an airplane

301
00:19:08,957 --> 00:19:12,860
the most obvious and perhaps the most important form of inequality would

302
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:18,259
already have disappeared. If it once became general, wealth would confer no distinction.

303
00:19:18,259 --> 00:19:22,457
It was possible, no doubt, to imagine a society in which wealth, in the sense of

304
00:19:22,457 --> 00:19:26,479
personal possessions and luxuries, should be evenly distributed, while power

305
00:19:26,479 --> 00:19:31,580
remained in the hands of a small privileged cast But in practice such a society could not

306
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:33,020
long remain stable.

307
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:37,279
For if leisure and security were enjoyed by all alike, the great massive human

308
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:41,180
beings were normally stupefied by poverty would become literate and would

309
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,900
learn to think for themselves; and when once they had done this, they would

310
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:48,919
sooner or later realize that the privileged minority had no function, and

311
00:19:48,919 --> 00:19:50,419
they would sweep it away.

312
00:19:50,419 --> 00:19:56,119
In the long run, a hierarchical society was only possible on the basis of poverty and ignorance.

313
00:19:56,119 --> 00:19:59,900
To return to the agricultural past, as some thinkers about the beginning of the

314
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:03,797
20th century dreamed of doing, was not a practicable solution.

315
00:20:03,797 --> 00:20:06,979
It conflicted with the tendency towards mechanization which had become

316
00:20:06,979 --> 00:20:11,000
quasi-instinctive throughout almost the whole world, and moreover, any country

317
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,020
which remained industrially backward was helpless in a military sense and was

318
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:20,718
bound to be dominated, directly or indirectly, by its more advanced rivals.

319
00:20:20,718 --> 00:20:24,080
Nor was it a satisfactory solution to keep the masses in poverty by

320
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:25,878
restricting the output of goods.

321
00:20:25,878 --> 00:20:29,957
This happens to a great extent during the final phase of capitalism, roughly

322
00:20:29,957 --> 00:20:34,819
between 1920 and 1940.. The economy of many countries was allowed to stagnate,

323
00:20:34,819 --> 00:20:39,378
land went out of cultivation, capital equipment was not added to, great blocks

324
00:20:39,378 --> 00:20:43,819
of the population were prevented from working and kept half alive by State charity.

325
00:20:43,819 --> 00:20:47,840
But this, too, entailed military weakness, and since the privations it inflicted

326
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:51,860
were obviously unnecessary, it made opposition inevitable. The problem was

327
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:56,360
how to keep the wheels of industry turning without increasing the real wealth of the world.

328
00:20:56,360 --> 00:21:00,797
Goods must be produced, but they must not be distributed. And in practice the only

329
00:21:00,797 --> 00:21:04,218
way of achieving this was by continuous warfare.

330
00:21:04,218 --> 00:21:08,297
The essential act of war is destruction, not necessarily of human lives, but of

331
00:21:08,297 --> 00:21:12,319
the products of human labor War is a way of shattering to pieces, or

332
00:21:12,319 --> 00:21:16,218
pouring into the stratosphere, or sinking in the depths of the sea, materials which

333
00:21:16,218 --> 00:21:20,000
might otherwise be used to make the masses too comfortable, and hence, in the

334
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,919
long run, too intelligent.

335
00:21:21,919 --> 00:21:25,939
Even when weapons of war are not actually destroyed, their manufacturer is

336
00:21:25,939 --> 00:21:29,419
still a convenient way of expending Labor power without producing anything

337
00:21:29,419 --> 00:21:33,919
that could be consumed the Floating Fortress, for example, has locked up in it

338
00:21:33,919 --> 00:21:37,878
the labor that would build several hundred cargo ships. Ultimately it is

339
00:21:37,878 --> 00:21:41,297
scrapped as obsolete, never having brought any material benefit to anybody,

340
00:21:41,297 --> 00:21:45,259
and with further enormous labors and other Floating fortresses built.

341
00:21:45,259 --> 00:21:48,919
In principle the war effort is always so planned as to eat up any surplus that

342
00:21:48,919 --> 00:21:52,340
might exist after meeting the bare needs of the population.

343
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:56,058
In practice the needs of the population are always underestimated, with the

344
00:21:56,058 --> 00:21:59,297
result that there is a chronic shortage of half the necessities of life;

345
00:21:59,297 --> 00:22:01,939
but this is looked on as an advantage.

346
00:22:01,939 --> 00:22:05,540
It is deliberate policy to keep even the favored groups somewhere near the brink

347
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:09,500
of hardship, because a general state of scarcity increases the importance of

348
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:14,419
small privileges and thus magnifies the distinction between one group and another.

349
00:22:14,419 --> 00:22:18,200
By the standards of the early 20th century, even a member of the Inner Party

350
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:20,957
lives an austere, laborious kind of life.

351
00:22:20,957 --> 00:22:25,099
Nevertheless, the few luxuries that he does enjoy— —his large well-appointed flat,

352
00:22:25,099 --> 00:22:29,000
the better texture of his clothes, the better quality of his food and drink and

353
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:34,040
tobacco is two or three servants, his private motor car or helicopter— —set him

354
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:37,400
in a different world from a member of the Outer Party, and the members of the

355
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:40,939
Outer Party have a similar advantage in comparison with the submerged masses

356
00:22:40,939 --> 00:22:42,680
whom we call 'the proles'.

357
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:46,700
The social atmosphere is that of a besieged city, where the position of a

358
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:50,180
lump of horse flesh makes the difference between wealth and poverty.

359
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:53,599
And at the same time the consciousness of being at war, and therefore in danger,

360
00:22:53,599 --> 00:22:57,680
makes the handing over of all power to a small cast seem the natural, unavoidable

361
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:00,500
condition of survival.

362
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:04,457
War, it will be seen accomplishes the necessary destruction, but accomplishes

363
00:23:04,457 --> 00:23:07,040
it in a psychologically acceptable way.

364
00:23:07,040 --> 00:23:10,279
In principle it would be quite simple to waste to the surplus labor of the world

365
00:23:10,279 --> 00:23:14,000
by building temples and pyramids, by digging holes and filling them up again,

366
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:18,439
or even by producing vast quantities of goods and then setting fire to them. But

367
00:23:18,439 --> 00:23:23,659
this would provide only the economic and not the emotional basis for a hierarchical society.

368
00:23:23,659 --> 00:23:27,860
What is concerned here is not the morale of masses, whose attitude is unimportant

369
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:32,000
so long as they are kept steadily at work, but the morale of the Party itself.

370
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,020
Even the humblest Party member is expected to be competent, industrious and

371
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:39,740
even intelligent within narrow limits, but it is also necessary that he should

372
00:23:39,740 --> 00:23:43,878
be a credulous and ignorant fanatic whose prevailing moods of fear, hatred,

373
00:23:43,878 --> 00:23:46,700
adulation and orgiastic triumph.

374
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:51,619
In other words it is necessary that he should have the mentality appropriate to a state of war.

375
00:23:51,619 --> 00:23:55,520
It does not matter whether the war is actually happening, and, since no decisive

376
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:59,659
victory is possible, it does not matter whether the war is going well or badly.

377
00:23:59,659 --> 00:24:04,700
All that is needed is that a state of war should exist splitting of the intelligence which the

378
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:08,419
Party requires of its members, and which is more easily achieved in an atmosphere

379
00:24:08,419 --> 00:24:12,860
of war, is now almost universal, but the higher up the ranks one goes, the more

380
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:14,240
marked it becomes.

381
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:19,580
It is precisely in the Inner Party that war hysteria and hatred of the enemy are strongest.

382
00:24:19,580 --> 00:24:23,240
In his capacity as an administrator, it is often necessary for a member of the

383
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:27,619
uni Party to know that this or that item of war news is untruthful, and he may

384
00:24:27,619 --> 00:24:31,580
often be aware that the entire war is spurious and is either not happening or

385
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:35,119
is being waged for purposes quite other than the declared ones:

386
00:24:35,119 --> 00:24:39,080
but such knowledge is easily neutralized by the technique of double think

387
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:42,919
Meanwhile no Inner Party member waivers for an instant in his mystical belief

388
00:24:42,919 --> 00:24:47,360
that the war is real, and that it is bound to end victoriously, with Oceania

389
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:50,840
the undisputed master of the entire world.

390
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:55,759
All members of the Inner Party believe in this coming conquest as an article of faith

391
00:24:55,759 --> 00:24:59,599
to be achieved either by gradually acquiring more and more territory and so

392
00:24:59,599 --> 00:25:02,718
building up an overwhelming preponderance of power, or by the

393
00:25:02,718 --> 00:25:05,718
discovery of some new and unanswerable weapon.

394
00:25:05,718 --> 00:25:09,740
The search for new weapons continues unceasingly, and is one of the very few

395
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:15,137
remaining activities in which the inventive or speculative type of mind can find any outlet.

396
00:25:15,137 --> 00:25:20,360
In Oceania at the present day, Science, in the old sense, has almost ceased to exist.

397
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:23,240
In Newspeak there is no word for 'Science'.

398
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:26,599
The empirical method of thought, on which all the scientific achievements of the

399
00:25:26,599 --> 00:25:31,279
past were founded, is opposed to the most fundamental principles of inksock

400
00:25:31,279 --> 00:25:34,878
And even technological progress only happens when its products can in some

401
00:25:34,878 --> 00:25:37,878
way be used for the diminution of human liberty.

402
00:25:37,878 --> 00:25:41,957
In all the useful arts the world is either standing still or going backwards.

403
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:45,919
The fields are cultivated with horsepower while books are written by machinery.

404
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:49,159
But in matters of vital importance meaning in effect, war and police

405
00:25:49,159 --> 00:25:54,200
espionage— —the empirical approach is still encouraged, or at least tolerated.

406
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:57,919
The two aims of the Party are to conquer the whole surface of the earth and to

407
00:25:57,919 --> 00:26:01,759
extinguish once and for all the possibility of Independence thought.

408
00:26:01,759 --> 00:26:05,718
There are therefore two great problems which the Party is concerned to solve.

409
00:26:05,718 --> 00:26:09,979
One is hard to discover, against his will, what another human being is thinking, and

410
00:26:09,979 --> 00:26:12,680
the other is how to kill several hundred million people in a few seconds without

411
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:16,939
giving warning beforehand insofar as scientific research still

412
00:26:16,939 --> 00:26:19,457
continues, this is its subject matter.

413
00:26:19,457 --> 00:26:23,000
The scientist of today is either a mixture of psychologist and inquisitor,

414
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:26,599
studying with real ordinary minuteness the meaning of facial expressions,

415
00:26:26,599 --> 00:26:30,619
gestures and tones of voice, and testing the truth producing effects of drugs,

416
00:26:30,619 --> 00:26:35,957
shock therapy, hypnosis and physical torture; or he is chemist, physicist or biologist

417
00:26:35,957 --> 00:26:41,540
concerned only with such branches of his special subject as irrelevant to the taking of life.

418
00:26:41,540 --> 00:26:45,259
In the vast laboratories of the Ministry of Peace, and in the experimental

419
00:26:45,259 --> 00:26:49,400
stations hidden in the Brazilian forests, or in the Australian desert, or on lost

420
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:53,779
islands of the Antarctic, the teams of experts are inter-fatigably at work.

421
00:26:53,779 --> 00:26:58,099
Some are concerned simply with planning the logistics of future wars; others

422
00:26:58,099 --> 00:27:02,479
devise larger and larger rocket bombs, more and more powerful explosives, and

423
00:27:02,479 --> 00:27:07,040
more and more impenetrable armor plating; others search for new and deadlier gases,

424
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:11,000
or for soluble poisons capable of being produced in such quantities as to

425
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:14,479
destroy the vegetation of whole continents, or for breeds of disease

426
00:27:14,479 --> 00:27:19,457
germs immunized against all possible antibodies; others strive to produce a vehicle that

427
00:27:19,457 --> 00:27:23,058
shall bore its way under the soil like a submarine under the water, or an airplane

428
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:27,319
is independent of its base as a sailing ship; others explore even remote

429
00:27:27,319 --> 00:27:31,520
possibilities such as focusing the sun's rays through lenses suspended thousands

430
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:35,779
of kilometers away in space, or producing artificial earthquakes and tidal waves

431
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:40,099
by tapping the heat at the earth's center But none of these projects ever comes

432
00:27:40,099 --> 00:27:43,759
anywhere near realization and none of the three super States ever gains a

433
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:45,797
significant lead on the others.

434
00:27:45,797 --> 00:27:49,279
What is more remarkable is that all three powers already possess, in the

435
00:27:49,279 --> 00:27:52,400
atomic bomb, a weapon far more powerful than any of that their present

436
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:54,797
researchers are likely to discover.

437
00:27:54,797 --> 00:27:58,058
Although the Party, according to its habit, claims the invention for itself,

438
00:27:58,058 --> 00:28:02,779
atomic bombs first appeared as early as the 1940s and were first used on a large

439
00:28:02,779 --> 00:28:05,119
scale about 10 years later.

440
00:28:05,119 --> 00:28:09,319
At that time some hundreds of bombs were dropped on industrial centers chiefly in

441
00:28:09,319 --> 00:28:12,740
European Russia, Western Europe and North America.

442
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:15,860
The effect was to convince the ruling groups of all countries that a few more

443
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:20,599
atomic bombs would mean the end of organized society, and hence of their own power.

444
00:28:20,599 --> 00:28:24,740
Thereafter, although no formal agreement was ever made or hinted at, no more bombs

445
00:28:24,740 --> 00:28:28,580
were dropped. All three powers merely continued to produce atomic bombs and

446
00:28:28,580 --> 00:28:33,619
store them up against the decisive opportunity which they all believe will come sooner or later.

447
00:28:33,619 --> 00:28:38,360
And meanwhile the art of war has remained almost stationary for 30 or 40 years.

448
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:42,259
Helicopters are more used than they were formally bombing plants have been

449
00:28:42,259 --> 00:28:45,979
largely superseded by self-propelled projectiles, and the fragile movable

450
00:28:45,979 --> 00:28:49,580
battleship has given way to the almost unsinkable Floating Fortress;

451
00:28:49,580 --> 00:28:52,279
but otherwise there has been little development.

452
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:56,360
The tank, the submarine, the torpedo, the machine gun even the rifle and the hand

453
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:57,979
grenade are still in use.

454
00:28:57,979 --> 00:29:01,040
And in spite of the endless slaughters reported in the press and on the

455
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:04,759
telescreens, the desperate battles of earlier wars, in which hundreds of

456
00:29:04,759 --> 00:29:10,637
thousands or even millions of men were often killed in a few weeks, have never been repeated.

457
00:29:10,637 --> 00:29:14,360
None of the three super States ever attempt any maneuver which involves the

458
00:29:14,360 --> 00:29:20,240
risk of serious defeat whenever any large operation is undertaken, it is usually a surprise

459
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,919
attack against an ally.

460
00:29:21,919 --> 00:29:25,580
The strategy that all three powers are following, or pretend to themselves that

461
00:29:25,580 --> 00:29:27,979
they are following, is the same.

462
00:29:27,979 --> 00:29:32,000
The plan is, by a combination of fighting, bargaining and well-timed strokes of

463
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:36,137
treachery, to acquire a ring of bases completely encircling one or other of

464
00:29:36,137 --> 00:29:40,520
the rival states, and then to sign a pact of friendship with that rival and remain

465
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:44,058
on peaceful terms for so many years as to allow suspicion to sleep.

466
00:29:44,058 --> 00:29:47,840
During this time rockets loaded with atomic bombs can be assembled at all the

467
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:52,279
strategic spots; finally they will all be fired simultaneously, with effects so

468
00:29:52,279 --> 00:29:55,040
devastating as to make retaliation impossible.

469
00:29:55,040 --> 00:29:58,099
It will then be time to sign a pact of friendship with the remaining world

470
00:29:58,099 --> 00:30:00,979
power in preparation for another attack.

471
00:30:00,979 --> 00:30:06,500
This scheme, it is hardly necessary to say, is a mere daydream, impossible realization

472
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:11,718
Moreover, no fighting ever occurs except in the disputed areas around the Equator and the Pole:

473
00:30:11,718 --> 00:30:14,900
no invasion of enemy territory is ever undertaken.

474
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:19,939
This explains the fact that in some places the frontiers between the super states are arbitrary.

475
00:30:19,939 --> 00:30:23,360
Eurasia, for example, could easily conquer the British Isles, which are

476
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:28,099
geographically part of Europe, or on the other hand it would be possible for Oceania to push its

477
00:30:28,099 --> 00:30:31,939
frontiers to the Rhine or even to the Vistula. But this would violate the

478
00:30:31,939 --> 00:30:35,659
principle, followed on all sides though never formulated, of cultural integrity.

479
00:30:35,659 --> 00:30:39,797
If Oceania were to conquer the areas that used once to be known as France and

480
00:30:39,797 --> 00:30:44,119
Germany, it would be necessary either to exterminate the inhabitants, a task of

481
00:30:44,119 --> 00:30:47,599
great physical difficulty, or to assimilate a population of about 100

482
00:30:47,599 --> 00:30:53,000
million people, who, so far as technical development goes, are roughly on the Oceanic level.

483
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:57,137
The problem is the same for all three super states It is absolutely necessary

484
00:30:57,137 --> 00:31:00,740
to their structure that there should be no contact with foreigners, except, to a

485
00:31:00,740 --> 00:31:05,058
limited extent, with war prisoners and colored slaves. Even the official ally of

486
00:31:05,058 --> 00:31:08,297
the moment is always regarded with the darkest suspicion.

487
00:31:08,297 --> 00:31:12,740
War prisoners apart, the average citizen of Oceania never sets eyes on a citizen

488
00:31:12,740 --> 00:31:17,360
of either Eurasia or East Asia and he has forbidden the knowledge of foreign languages.

489
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:20,419
If he were allowed contact with foreigners he would discover that they

490
00:31:20,419 --> 00:31:25,279
are creatures similar to himself and that most of what he has been told about them is lies

491
00:31:25,279 --> 00:31:28,939
sealed world in which he lives would be broken, and the fear, hatred and

492
00:31:28,939 --> 00:31:32,297
self-righteousness on which his morale depends might evaporate.

493
00:31:32,297 --> 00:31:36,500
It is therefore realized on all sides that however often Persia, or Egypt, or

494
00:31:36,500 --> 00:31:40,819
Java or Salon may change hands, the main frontiers must never be crossed by

495
00:31:40,819 --> 00:31:44,020
anything except bombs.

496
00:31:44,180 --> 00:31:48,439
Under this lies effect never mentioned aloud, but tacitly understood and acted

497
00:31:48,439 --> 00:31:53,659
upon: namely, that the conditions of life in all three super states are very much the same.

498
00:31:53,659 --> 00:31:58,040
In Oceania the prevailing philosophy is called insock in Eurasia it is called

499
00:31:58,040 --> 00:32:02,540
Neo-Bolshevism, and in East Asia it is called by a Chinese name usually

500
00:32:02,540 --> 00:32:06,979
translated as death worship but perhaps better rendered as Obliteration of the Self.

501
00:32:06,979 --> 00:32:10,340
The citizen of Oceania is not allowed to know anything of the tenets of the other

502
00:32:10,340 --> 00:32:14,479
two philosophies, but he is taught to execrate them as barbarous outrages upon

503
00:32:14,479 --> 00:32:17,180
morality and common sense.

504
00:32:17,180 --> 00:32:20,599
Actually the three philosophies are barely distinguishable, and the social

505
00:32:20,599 --> 00:32:24,020
systems which they support are not distinguishable at all.

506
00:32:24,020 --> 00:32:27,558
Everywhere there is the same pyramidal structure, the same worship of

507
00:32:27,558 --> 00:32:32,840
semi-divine leader, the same economy existing by and for continuous warfare.

508
00:32:32,840 --> 00:32:36,919
It follows that the three super States not only cannot conquer one another, but

509
00:32:36,919 --> 00:32:41,297
would gain no advantage by doing so. On the contrary, so long as they remain in

510
00:32:41,297 --> 00:32:45,020
conflict they prop one another up, like three sheaves of corn.

511
00:32:45,020 --> 00:32:49,159
And, as usual, the ruling groups of all three powers are simultaneously aware

512
00:32:49,159 --> 00:32:51,319
and unaware of what they are doing.

513
00:32:51,319 --> 00:32:54,860
Their lives are dedicated to world conquest, but they also know that it is

514
00:32:54,860 --> 00:32:58,580
necessary that the war should continue everlastingly and without victory.

515
00:32:58,580 --> 00:33:02,297
Meanwhile the fact that there is no danger of conquest makes possible the

516
00:33:02,297 --> 00:33:05,840
denial of reality which is the special feature of ingstock and its rival

517
00:33:05,840 --> 00:33:09,797
systems of thought. Here it is necessary to repeat what has been said earlier,

518
00:33:09,797 --> 00:33:15,378
that by becoming continuous war has fundamentally changed its character.

519
00:33:15,378 --> 00:33:19,340
In past ages of war, almost by definition, was something that sooner or later came

520
00:33:19,340 --> 00:33:23,599
to an end, usually an unmistakable victory or defeat.

521
00:33:23,599 --> 00:33:27,860
In the past, also, war was one of the main instruments by which human societies

522
00:33:27,860 --> 00:33:30,500
were kept in touch with physical reality.

523
00:33:30,500 --> 00:33:34,218
All rulers in all ages have tried to impose a false view of the world upon

524
00:33:34,218 --> 00:33:37,457
their followers, but they could not afford to encourage any illusions that

525
00:33:37,457 --> 00:33:40,400
tended to impair military efficiency.

526
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:43,637
So long as defeat meant the loss of independence, or some other results

527
00:33:43,637 --> 00:33:48,740
generally held to be undesirable, the precautions against defeat had to be serious.

528
00:33:48,740 --> 00:33:53,119
Physical facts could not be ignored. In philosophy, or religion, or ethics, or

529
00:33:53,119 --> 00:33:57,500
politics, two and two might make five, but when one was designing a gun or an

530
00:33:57,500 --> 00:33:59,297
airplane they had to make four.

531
00:33:59,297 --> 00:34:03,080
Inefficient nations were always conquered sooner or later, and the

532
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:05,900
struggle for efficiency was inimical to illusions.

533
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:09,319
Moreover, to be efficient it was necessary to be able to learn from the

534
00:34:09,319 --> 00:34:13,457
past, which meant having a fairly accurate idea of what had happened in the past.

535
00:34:13,457 --> 00:34:17,240
Newspapers and history books were, of course, always colored and biased, but

536
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:21,259
falsification of the kind that is practiced today would have been impossible

537
00:34:21,259 --> 00:34:25,520
Moore was the sure safeguard of sanity, and so far as the ruling classes were

538
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:29,058
concerned it was probably the most important of all safeguards.

539
00:34:29,058 --> 00:34:34,400
While wars could be won or lost, no ruling class could be completely irresponsible.

540
00:34:34,400 --> 00:34:39,020
But when war becomes literally continuous, it also ceases to be dangerous.

541
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:42,740
When war is continuous there is no such thing as military necessity.

542
00:34:42,740 --> 00:34:48,080
Technical progress consists into the most palpable facts can be denied or disregarded.

543
00:34:48,080 --> 00:34:51,378
As we have seen researchers that could be called scientific are still carried

544
00:34:51,378 --> 00:34:55,580
out for the purposes of war, but they are essentially a kind of daydreaming, and

545
00:34:55,580 --> 00:34:58,218
their failure to show results is not important.

546
00:34:58,218 --> 00:35:02,599
Efficiency, even military efficiency, is no longer needed. Nothing is efficient in

547
00:35:02,599 --> 00:35:05,119
Oceania except the Thought Police.

548
00:35:05,119 --> 00:35:09,439
Since each of the three super States is unconquerable, each year is in effect a

549
00:35:09,439 --> 00:35:13,759
separate universe within which almost any perversion of thought can be safely practiced

550
00:35:13,759 --> 00:35:17,779
Reality only exerts its pressure through the needs of everyday life— —the need to

551
00:35:17,779 --> 00:35:21,680
eat and drink, to get shelter and clothing, to avoid swallowing poison or

552
00:35:21,680 --> 00:35:24,740
stepping out of top story windows under the like.

553
00:35:24,740 --> 00:35:29,058
Between life and death between physical pleasure and physical pain, there is

554
00:35:29,058 --> 00:35:32,840
still a distinction, but that is all. Cut off from contact with the outer world,

555
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:37,759
and with the past, the citizen of Oceania is like a man in interstellar space, who

556
00:35:37,759 --> 00:35:41,058
has no way of knowing which direction is up and which is down.

557
00:35:41,058 --> 00:35:44,900
The rulers of such a state are absolute, as the Pharaohs or the Caesars could not

558
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:48,619
be. They are obliged to prevent their followers from starving to death in

559
00:35:48,619 --> 00:35:52,400
numbers large enough to be inconvenient, and they are obliged to remain at the

560
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:56,000
same low level of military technique as their rivals; but once that minimum is

561
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:00,558
achieved, they can twist reality into whatever shape they choose.

562
00:36:00,558 --> 00:36:05,599
The war, therefore, if we judge it by the standards of previous wars, is merely an imposter

563
00:36:05,599 --> 00:36:09,200
It is like the battles between certain ruminant animals whose horns are set at

564
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:12,378
such an angle that they are incapable of hurting one another.

565
00:36:12,378 --> 00:36:16,340
But though it is unreal it is not meaningless. It heats up the surplus of

566
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:20,119
consumable goods, and it helps to preserve the special mental atmosphere

567
00:36:20,119 --> 00:36:24,680
that a hierarchical society needs more it will be seen as now a purely internal

568
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:29,119
affair. In the past, the ruling groups of all countries, although they might

569
00:36:29,119 --> 00:36:32,058
recognize their common interest and therefore limit the destructiveness of

570
00:36:32,058 --> 00:36:36,979
war, did fight against one another, and the victor always plundered the vanquished.

571
00:36:36,979 --> 00:36:41,000
In our own day they are not fighting against one another at all. The war is

572
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:44,957
waged by each ruling group against its own subjects, and the object of the war

573
00:36:44,957 --> 00:36:50,180
is not to make or prevent conquests of territory, but to keep the structure of society intact.

574
00:36:50,180 --> 00:36:53,957
The very word 'war', therefore, has become misleading.

575
00:36:53,957 --> 00:36:57,259
It would probably be accurate to say that by becoming continuous war has

576
00:36:57,259 --> 00:37:01,457
ceased to exist. The peculiar pressure that it exerted on human beings between

577
00:37:01,457 --> 00:37:05,119
the Neolithic Age and the early 20th century has disappeared and been

578
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:07,400
replaced by something quite different.

579
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:11,000
The effect would be much the same if the three super States instead of fighting

580
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:16,279
one another, should agree to live in perpetual peace, each inviolet within its own boundaries.

581
00:37:16,279 --> 00:37:19,819
For in that case each would still be a self-contained universe, freed forever

582
00:37:19,819 --> 00:37:22,580
from the sobering influence of external danger.

583
00:37:22,580 --> 00:37:26,900
A piece that was truly permanent would be the same as a permanent war. This—

584
00:37:26,900 --> 00:37:30,319
—although the vast majority of Party members understand it only in a

585
00:37:30,319 --> 00:37:36,279
shallower sense— —is the inner meaning of the Party slogan: War is Peace.

586
00:37:36,279 --> 00:37:39,378
Winston stopped reading for a moment.

587
00:37:39,378 --> 00:37:42,797
Somewhere in remote distance a rocket bomb thundered.

588
00:37:42,797 --> 00:37:46,520
The blissful feeling of being alone with the forbidden book, in a room with no

589
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:48,919
telescreen, had not worn off.

590
00:37:48,919 --> 00:37:52,700
Solitude and safety were physical sensations, mixed up somehow with the

591
00:37:52,700 --> 00:37:56,840
tiredness of his body, the softness of the chair, the touch of the faint breeze

592
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:59,419
from the window that played upon his cheek.

593
00:37:59,419 --> 00:38:03,080
The book fascinated him, or more exactly it reassured him.

594
00:38:03,080 --> 00:38:07,159
In a sense it told him nothing that was new, but that was part of the attraction.

595
00:38:07,159 --> 00:38:11,119
It said what he would have said, if it had been possible for him to set his

596
00:38:11,119 --> 00:38:12,979
scattered thoughts in order.

597
00:38:12,979 --> 00:38:16,637
It was the product of a mind similar to his own, but enormously more powerful,

598
00:38:16,637 --> 00:38:21,200
more systematic, less fear-ridden The best books, he perceived, are those

599
00:38:21,200 --> 00:38:23,240
that tell you what you know already.

600
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:27,319
He had just turned back to Chapter one when he heard Julia's footstep on the

601
00:38:27,319 --> 00:38:30,137
stair and started out of his chair to meet her.

602
00:38:30,137 --> 00:38:34,520
She dumped her brown tool bag on the floor and flung herself into his arms. It

603
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:37,580
was more than a week since they had seen one another.

604
00:38:37,580 --> 00:38:42,020
'I've got the book,'' he said as they disentangled themselves.

605
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:46,700
'Oh, you've got it? Good,' she said without much interest, and almost immediately

606
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:50,840
knelt down beside the oil stove to make the coffee.

607
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:54,860
They did not return to the subject until they had been in bed for half an hour.

608
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:58,819
The evening was just cool enough to make it worthwhile to pull up the counterpane.

609
00:38:58,819 --> 00:39:02,297
From below came the familiar sound of singing and the scrape of boots on the

610
00:39:02,297 --> 00:39:06,680
flagstones. The brawny red-armed woman whom Winston had seen there on his first

611
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:09,020
visit was almost a fixture in the yard.

612
00:39:09,020 --> 00:39:12,500
There seemed to be no hour of daylight when she was not marching to and fro

613
00:39:12,500 --> 00:39:15,919
between the wash tub and the line, alternately gagging herself with clothes

614
00:39:15,919 --> 00:39:19,340
pigs and breaking forth into lusty song.

615
00:39:19,340 --> 00:39:24,439
Julia had settled down on her side and seemed to be already on the point of falling asleep.

616
00:39:24,439 --> 00:39:27,500
He reached out for the book, which was lying on the floor, and sat up against

617
00:39:27,500 --> 00:39:32,599
the Bed Head We must read it,' he said. 'You too. All

618
00:39:32,599 --> 00:39:35,000
members of the Brotherhood have to read it.'

619
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:37,040
'You read it,' she said with her eyes shut.

620
00:39:37,040 --> 00:39:42,378
'Read it aloud. That's the best way. Then you can explain it to me as you go.'

621
00:39:42,378 --> 00:39:46,580
The clock's hands said six, meaning eighteen. They had three or four hours

622
00:39:46,580 --> 00:39:52,819
ahead of them. He propped the book against his knees and began reading: Chapter one

623
00:39:52,819 --> 00:39:55,457
Ignorance is Strength.

624
00:39:55,457 --> 00:39:59,240
Throughout recorded time, and probably since the end of the Neolithic Age, there

625
00:39:59,240 --> 00:40:02,900
have been three kinds of people in the world, the High, the Middle and the Low.

626
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:06,797
They have been subdivided in many ways, they have borne countless different

627
00:40:06,797 --> 00:40:10,457
names, and their relative numbers, as well as their attitude towards one another,

628
00:40:10,457 --> 00:40:14,900
have varied from age to age: but the essential structure of society has never

629
00:40:14,900 --> 00:40:19,759
altered. Even after enormous upheavals and seemingly irrevocable changes, the

630
00:40:19,759 --> 00:40:23,419
same pattern has always reasserted itself, just as a gyroscope will always

631
00:40:23,419 --> 00:40:28,279
return to equilibrium, however far it has pushed one way or the other.

632
00:40:28,279 --> 00:40:31,520
'Julia, are you awake?' said Winston.

633
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:37,340
'Yes, my love, I'm listening. Go on. It's marvelous He continued reading:

634
00:40:37,340 --> 00:40:41,419
The aims of these three groups are entirely irreconcilable. The aim of the

635
00:40:41,419 --> 00:40:45,020
High is to remain where they are. The aim of the Middle is to change places with

636
00:40:45,020 --> 00:40:48,200
the High. The aim of the Low, when they have a name

637
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:51,797
for it is an abiding characteristic of the law that they are too much crushed

638
00:40:51,797 --> 00:40:56,297
by drudgery to be more than intermittently conscious of anything outside their daily lives—

639
00:40:56,297 --> 00:41:01,099
—is to abolish all distinctions and create a society in which all men shall be equal.

640
00:41:01,099 --> 00:41:04,580
Thus throughout history a struggle which is the same in its main outlines it

641
00:41:04,580 --> 00:41:06,619
occurs over and over again.

642
00:41:06,619 --> 00:41:10,878
For long periods the High seemed to be securely in power, but sooner or later

643
00:41:10,878 --> 00:41:13,939
there always comes a moment when they lose either their belief in themselves

644
00:41:13,939 --> 00:41:17,540
or their capacity to govern efficiently, or both.

645
00:41:17,540 --> 00:41:21,020
They are then overthrown by the Middle, who enlist the law on their side by

646
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:24,797
pretending to them that they are fighting for liberty and justice.

647
00:41:24,797 --> 00:41:27,740
As soon as they have reached their objective, the Middle thrusts the Low

648
00:41:27,740 --> 00:41:32,119
back into their older position of servitude, and themselves has become the High.

649
00:41:32,119 --> 00:41:35,360
Presently a new Middle group splits off from one of the other groups, or from

650
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:38,540
both of them, and the struggle begins over again.

651
00:41:38,540 --> 00:41:42,680
Of the three groups, only the lower never even temporarily successful in achieving

652
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:46,700
their aims. It would be an exaggeration to say that throughout history there has

653
00:41:46,700 --> 00:41:49,099
been no progress of a material kind.

654
00:41:49,099 --> 00:41:53,058
Even today, in a period of decline, the average human being is physically better

655
00:41:53,058 --> 00:41:57,500
off than he was a few centuries ago. But no advance in wealth, no softening of

656
00:41:57,500 --> 00:42:02,479
manners, no reform or revolution has ever brought human equality a millimeter nearer.

657
00:42:02,479 --> 00:42:06,200
From the point of view of the Low, no historic change has ever meant much more

658
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:09,500
than a change in the name of their masters.

659
00:42:09,500 --> 00:42:14,599
By the late 19th century the recurrence of this patent had become obvious to many observers

660
00:42:14,599 --> 00:42:17,840
they then Rose schools of thinkers who interpreted history as a cyclical

661
00:42:17,840 --> 00:42:22,878
process and claimed to show that inequality was the unalterable law of human life.

662
00:42:22,878 --> 00:42:26,659
This doctrine, of course, had always had its adherence but in the manner in which

663
00:42:26,659 --> 00:42:29,540
it was now put forward there was a significant change.

664
00:42:29,540 --> 00:42:33,259
In the past the need for a hierarchical form of society had been the doctrine

665
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:35,000
specifically of the High.

666
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:38,360
It had been preached by kings and aristocrats and by the priest's lawyers

667
00:42:38,360 --> 00:42:42,558
and the like who were parasitical upon them, and it had generally been softened

668
00:42:42,558 --> 00:42:47,119
by promises of compensation in an imaginary world beyond the grave.

669
00:42:47,119 --> 00:42:50,840
The Middle, so long as it was struggling for power, had always made use of such

670
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:52,819
terms as freedom, justice and fraternity.

671
00:42:52,819 --> 00:42:56,900
Now, however, the concept of human brotherhood began to be assailed by

672
00:42:56,900 --> 00:43:02,360
people who were not yet in positions of command, but merely hoped to be so before long.

673
00:43:02,360 --> 00:43:05,779
In the past the Middle had made revolutions under the banner of equality,

674
00:43:05,779 --> 00:43:10,040
and then had established a fresh tyranny as soon as the old one was overthrown.

675
00:43:10,040 --> 00:43:13,240
The new Middle groups in effect proclaimed their tyranny beforehand.

676
00:43:13,240 --> 00:43:17,599
Socialism, a theory of which appeared in the early 19th century and was the last

677
00:43:17,599 --> 00:43:20,840
link in a chain of thought stretching back to the slave rebellions of

678
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:25,520
antiquity, was still deeply infected by the Utopianism of past ages.

679
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:30,020
But in each variant of Socialism that appeared from about 1900 onwards the aim

680
00:43:30,020 --> 00:43:33,919
of establishing liberty and equality was more and more openly abandoned.

681
00:43:33,919 --> 00:43:37,400
The new movements which appeared in the middle years of the century ing soccer

682
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:42,020
in Oceania, Neo-Bolshevism in Eurasia death worship as it is commonly called,

683
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:46,700
in East Asia and the conscious aim of perpetuating unfreedom and inequality.

684
00:43:46,700 --> 00:43:50,180
These new movements, of course, grew out of the old ones intended to keep their

685
00:43:50,180 --> 00:43:52,759
names and pay lip service to their ideology.

686
00:43:52,759 --> 00:43:57,259
But the purpose of all of them was to arrest progress and freeze history at a chosen moment.

687
00:43:57,259 --> 00:44:01,400
The familiar pendulum swing was to happen once more, and then stop.

688
00:44:01,400 --> 00:44:06,020
As usual, the High were to be turned out by the Middle, who would then become the High;

689
00:44:06,020 --> 00:44:09,619
but this time, by conscious strategy, the High would be able to maintain their

690
00:44:09,619 --> 00:44:12,137
position permanently.

691
00:44:12,137 --> 00:44:15,319
The new doctrines arose partly because of the accumulation of historical

692
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:18,558
knowledge, and the growth of the historical sense, which had hardly

693
00:44:18,558 --> 00:44:21,080
existed before the 19th century.

694
00:44:21,080 --> 00:44:25,218
The cyclical movement of history was now intelligible, or appeared to be so;

695
00:44:25,218 --> 00:44:28,457
and if it was intelligible, then it was alterable.

696
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:32,419
But the principle underlying cause was that, as early as the beginning of the

697
00:44:32,419 --> 00:44:36,439
20th century, human equality had become technically possible.

698
00:44:36,439 --> 00:44:39,979
It was still true that men were not equal in their native talents and that

699
00:44:39,979 --> 00:44:44,360
functions had to be specialized in ways that favored some individuals against others;

700
00:44:44,360 --> 00:44:47,659
but there was no longer any real need for class distinctions or for large

701
00:44:47,659 --> 00:44:51,680
differences of wealth. In earlier ages, class distinctions had been not only

702
00:44:51,680 --> 00:44:53,659
inevitable but desirable.

703
00:44:53,659 --> 00:44:57,740
Inequality was the price of civilization With the development of machine

704
00:44:57,740 --> 00:45:00,020
production, however, the case was altered.

705
00:45:00,020 --> 00:45:04,040
Even if it was still necessary for human beings to do different kinds of work, it

706
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:07,819
was no longer necessary for them to live a different social or economic levels.

707
00:45:07,819 --> 00:45:11,058
Therefore, from the point of view of the new groups who are on the point of

708
00:45:11,058 --> 00:45:14,957
seizing power, human equality was no longer an ideal to be striven after, but

709
00:45:14,957 --> 00:45:19,637
a danger to be averted. In more primitive ages, when a just and peaceful society

710
00:45:19,637 --> 00:45:23,659
was in fact not possible, it had been fairly easy to believe it.

711
00:45:23,659 --> 00:45:27,200
The idea of an earthly paradise in which men should live together in a state of

712
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:30,740
brotherhood, without laws and without brute labor had haunted the human

713
00:45:30,740 --> 00:45:34,819
imagination for thousands of years. And this vision had had a certain hold even

714
00:45:34,819 --> 00:45:38,479
on the groups who actually profited by each historical change.

715
00:45:38,479 --> 00:45:42,319
The heirs of the French, English and American revolutions had partly believed

716
00:45:42,319 --> 00:45:46,159
in their own phrases about the rights of man, freedom of speech, equality before

717
00:45:46,159 --> 00:45:49,700
the law, and the like, and had even allowed their conduct to be influenced

718
00:45:49,700 --> 00:45:51,619
by them to some extent.

719
00:45:51,619 --> 00:45:55,340
But by the fourth decade of the 20th century all the main currents of

720
00:45:55,340 --> 00:45:57,680
political thought were authoritarian.

721
00:45:57,680 --> 00:46:02,479
The earthly paradise had been discredited at exactly the moment when it became realizable

722
00:46:02,479 --> 00:46:06,680
Every new political theory, by whatever name it called itself, led back to

723
00:46:06,680 --> 00:46:08,718
hierarchy and regimentation.

724
00:46:08,718 --> 00:46:13,159
And in the general hardening of outlook that set in around about 1930, practices

725
00:46:13,159 --> 00:46:17,058
which had been long abandoned, in some cases for hundreds of years— —imprisonment

726
00:46:17,058 --> 00:46:22,159
without trial, the use of war prisoners as slaves, public executions tortured to

727
00:46:22,159 --> 00:46:26,419
extract confessions, the use of hostages and the deportation of whole populations—

728
00:46:26,419 --> 00:46:30,378
—not only became common again, but were tolerated and even defended by people

729
00:46:30,378 --> 00:46:34,040
who considered themselves enlightened and progressive.

730
00:46:34,040 --> 00:46:38,000
It was only after a decade of national wars, civil wars, revolutions and

731
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:42,080
counter-revolutions in all parts of the world the dingsok and its rivals emerged

732
00:46:42,080 --> 00:46:45,020
as fully worked out of the political theories.

733
00:46:45,020 --> 00:46:48,680
But they had been foreshadowed by the various systems, generally called

734
00:46:48,680 --> 00:46:53,419
totalitarian, which had appeared earlier in the century, and the main outlines of

735
00:46:53,419 --> 00:46:57,080
the world which would emerge from the prevailing chaos had long been obvious.

736
00:46:57,080 --> 00:47:00,680
What kind of people would control this world had been equally obvious.

737
00:47:00,680 --> 00:47:04,637
The new aristocracy was made up for the most part of bureaucrats, scientists,

738
00:47:04,637 --> 00:47:09,860
technicians Trade union organizers publicity experts, sociologists, teachers,

739
00:47:09,860 --> 00:47:12,500
journalists and professional politicians.

740
00:47:12,500 --> 00:47:16,040
These people, whose origins lay in the salaried middle class and the upper

741
00:47:16,040 --> 00:47:19,218
grades of the working class, had been shaped and brought together by the

742
00:47:19,218 --> 00:47:22,759
barren world of monopoly industry and centralized government.

743
00:47:22,759 --> 00:47:26,360
As compared with their opposite numbers in past ages, they were less avaricious,

744
00:47:26,360 --> 00:47:30,680
less tempted by luxury, hungrier for pure power, and, above all, more conscious of

745
00:47:30,680 --> 00:47:33,979
what they were doing and more intent on crushing opposition.

746
00:47:33,979 --> 00:47:36,378
This last difference was cardinal.

747
00:47:36,378 --> 00:47:39,740
By comparison with that existing today, all the tyrannies of the past were

748
00:47:39,740 --> 00:47:43,520
half-hearted and inefficient. The ruling groups were always infected to some

749
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:48,020
extent by liberal ideas, and were content to leave loose ends everywhere, to regard

750
00:47:48,020 --> 00:47:52,340
only the overt act and to be uninterested in what their subjects were thinking.

751
00:47:52,340 --> 00:47:55,939
Even the Catholic Church of the Middle Ages was tolerant by modern standards.

752
00:47:55,939 --> 00:48:00,080
Part of the reason for this was that in the past no government had the power to

753
00:48:00,080 --> 00:48:02,779
keep its citizens under constant surveillance.

754
00:48:02,779 --> 00:48:07,218
The invention of print, however, made it easier to manipulate public opinion, and

755
00:48:07,218 --> 00:48:10,099
the film and the radio carried the process further.

756
00:48:10,099 --> 00:48:13,159
With the development of television, and the technical advance which made it

757
00:48:13,159 --> 00:48:15,740
possible to receive and transmit simultaneously on the same instrument,

758
00:48:15,740 --> 00:48:18,200
private life came to an end.

759
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:21,680
Every citizen, or at least every citizen important enough to be worth watching,

760
00:48:21,680 --> 00:48:25,700
could be kept for 24 hours a day under the eyes of the police and in the sound

761
00:48:25,700 --> 00:48:30,259
of official propaganda, with all other channels of communication closed.

762
00:48:30,259 --> 00:48:33,500
The possibility of enforcing not only complete obedience to the will of the

763
00:48:33,500 --> 00:48:40,218
State, but complete uniformity of opinion on all subjects, now existed for the first time.

764
00:48:40,218 --> 00:48:44,540
After the revolutionary period of the 50s and 60s society regrouped itself, as

765
00:48:44,540 --> 00:48:46,637
always, into High, Middle and Low.

766
00:48:46,637 --> 00:48:51,020
But the new High group, unlike all its forerunners, did not act upon instinct

767
00:48:51,020 --> 00:48:53,957
but knew what was needed to safeguard its position.

768
00:48:53,957 --> 00:48:59,000
It had long been realized that the only secure basis for oligarchy is collectivism.

769
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:03,020
Wealth and privilege are most easily defended when they are possessed jointly.

770
00:49:03,020 --> 00:49:06,259
The so-called 'abolition of private property' which took place in the middle

771
00:49:06,259 --> 00:49:10,159
years of the century meant, in effect, the concentration of property and far fewer

772
00:49:10,159 --> 00:49:13,457
hands than before: but with this difference, that the new

773
00:49:13,457 --> 00:49:16,400
owners were a group instead of a mass of individuals.

774
00:49:16,400 --> 00:49:21,080
Individually, no member of the Party owns anything, except petty personal belongings.

775
00:49:21,080 --> 00:49:24,680
Collectively, the Party owns everything in Oceania, because it controls

776
00:49:24,680 --> 00:49:28,040
everything, and disposes of the products as it thinks fit.

777
00:49:28,040 --> 00:49:31,400
In the years following the Revolution it was able to step into this commanding

778
00:49:31,400 --> 00:49:35,360
position almost unopposed, because the whole process was represented as an act

779
00:49:35,360 --> 00:49:40,878
of collectivization It had always been assumed that if the capitalist class were expropriated,

780
00:49:40,878 --> 00:49:46,279
Socialism must follow: and unquestionably the capitalists had been expropriated.

781
00:49:46,279 --> 00:49:50,718
Factories, mines, land, houses, transport— —everything had been taken away from them:

782
00:49:50,718 --> 00:49:54,619
and since these things were no longer private property, it followed that they

783
00:49:54,619 --> 00:49:57,797
must be public property insock which grew out of the earlier

784
00:49:57,797 --> 00:50:02,900
Socialist movement and inherited its phraseology, has in fact carried out the main item in

785
00:50:02,900 --> 00:50:06,319
the Socialist program with the result, foreseen and intended

786
00:50:06,319 --> 00:50:10,457
beforehand, that economic inequality has been made permanent.

787
00:50:10,457 --> 00:50:15,137
But the problems of perpetuating a hierarchical society go deeper than this.

788
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:19,099
There are only four ways in which a ruling group can fall from power.

789
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:22,759
Either it is conquered from without, or it governs so inefficiently that the

790
00:50:22,759 --> 00:50:26,957
masses are stirred to revolt, or it allows a strong and discontented Middle

791
00:50:26,957 --> 00:50:32,540
group to come into being, or it loses its own self-confidence and willingness to govern.

792
00:50:32,540 --> 00:50:37,040
These causes do not operate singly, and as a rule all four of them are present

793
00:50:37,040 --> 00:50:38,297
in some degree.

794
00:50:38,297 --> 00:50:43,457
A ruling class which could guard against all of them would remain in power permanently.

795
00:50:43,457 --> 00:50:48,939
Ultimately the determining factor is the mental attitude of the ruling class itself.

796
00:50:48,939 --> 00:50:52,759
After the middle of the present century, the first danger had in reality

797
00:50:52,759 --> 00:50:56,599
disappeared. Each of the three powers which now divide the world is in fact

798
00:50:56,599 --> 00:51:00,740
uncontrable and could only become conquerable through its slow demographic

799
00:51:00,740 --> 00:51:04,819
changes which a government with wide powers can easily avert. The second

800
00:51:04,819 --> 00:51:07,580
danger, also, is only a theoretical one.

801
00:51:07,580 --> 00:51:11,180
The masses never revolt of their own accord, and they never revolt merely

802
00:51:11,180 --> 00:51:12,860
because they were oppressed.

803
00:51:12,860 --> 00:51:17,000
Indeed, so long as they are not permitted to have standards of comparison, they

804
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:19,878
never even become aware that they are oppressed.

805
00:51:19,878 --> 00:51:24,378
The recurrent economic crises of past times were totally unnecessary and are

806
00:51:24,378 --> 00:51:28,457
not now permitted to happen, but other and equally large dislocations can and

807
00:51:28,457 --> 00:51:32,180
do happen without having political results, because there is no way in which

808
00:51:32,180 --> 00:51:34,759
discontent can become articulate.

809
00:51:34,759 --> 00:51:38,419
As for the problem of overproduction, which has been latent in our society

810
00:51:38,419 --> 00:51:42,319
since the development of machine technique, it is solved by the divisive

811
00:51:42,319 --> 00:51:47,540
continuous warfare C Chapter 3. which is also useful in keying up public morale

812
00:51:47,540 --> 00:51:49,700
to the necessary pitch.

813
00:51:49,700 --> 00:51:53,180
From the point of view of our present rule is therefore, the only genuine

814
00:51:53,180 --> 00:51:57,020
dangers of the splitting off of a new group of able underemployed power-hungry

815
00:51:57,020 --> 00:52:01,637
people, and the growth of liberalism and skepticism in their own ranks.

816
00:52:01,637 --> 00:52:04,520
The problem, that is to say, is educational.

817
00:52:04,520 --> 00:52:08,240
It is a problem of continuously molding the consciousness both of the directing

818
00:52:08,240 --> 00:52:12,378
group and of the larger executive group that lies immediately below it.

819
00:52:12,378 --> 00:52:17,360
The consciousness of the masses needs only to be influenced in a negative way.

820
00:52:17,360 --> 00:52:21,137
Given this background, one could infer, if one did not know it already, the general

821
00:52:21,137 --> 00:52:23,180
structure of Oceanic society.

822
00:52:23,180 --> 00:52:26,119
At the apex of the pyramid comes Big Brother.

823
00:52:26,119 --> 00:52:30,860
Big Brother is infallible and all-powerful Every success, every achievement, every

824
00:52:30,860 --> 00:52:35,540
victory, every scientific discovery, all knowledge, all wisdom, all happiness, all

825
00:52:35,540 --> 00:52:40,040
virtue, are held to issue directly from his leadership and inspiration.

826
00:52:40,040 --> 00:52:44,180
Nobody has ever seen Big Brother. He has a face on the hoardings, a voice on the

827
00:52:44,180 --> 00:52:48,680
telescreen. We may be reasonably sure that he will never die, and there is

828
00:52:48,680 --> 00:52:52,040
already considerable uncertainty as to when he was born.

829
00:52:52,040 --> 00:52:56,540
Big Brother is the guys in which the Party chooses to exhibit itself to the world.

830
00:52:56,540 --> 00:53:00,137
His function is to act as a focusing point for love, fear and reverence,

831
00:53:00,137 --> 00:53:05,180
emotions which are more easily felt towards an individual than towards an organization

832
00:53:05,180 --> 00:53:10,040
Below Big Brother comes the Inner Party, its numbers limited to six millions, or

833
00:53:10,040 --> 00:53:13,340
something less than two percent of the population of Oceania.

834
00:53:13,340 --> 00:53:17,058
Below the Inner Party comes the Outer Party, which, if the Inner Party is

835
00:53:17,058 --> 00:53:21,740
described as the brain of the State, may be justly likened to the hands. Below

836
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:24,797
that come the dumb masses whom we habitually refer to as 'the pros

837
00:53:24,797 --> 00:53:28,520
numbering perhaps 85 percent of the population.

838
00:53:28,520 --> 00:53:32,119
In the terms of our earlier classification, the pearls of the Low:

839
00:53:32,119 --> 00:53:35,297
for the slave population of the equatorial lands, who pass constantly

840
00:53:35,297 --> 00:53:40,040
from conqueror to conqueror, are not a permanent or necessary part of the structure.

841
00:53:40,040 --> 00:53:44,419
In principle, membership of these three groups is not hereditary. The child of

842
00:53:44,419 --> 00:53:48,137
the Inner Party parents is in theory not born into the Inner Party.

843
00:53:48,137 --> 00:53:53,240
Admission to either branch of the Party is by examination, taken at the age of 16.

844
00:53:53,240 --> 00:53:58,040
Nor is there any racial discrimination, or any Marx domination of one province by another.

845
00:53:58,040 --> 00:54:02,360
Jews, Negroes, South Americans of pure Indian blood are to be found in the

846
00:54:02,360 --> 00:54:06,080
highest ranks of the Party, and the administrators of any area are always

847
00:54:06,080 --> 00:54:08,779
drawn from the inhabitants of that area.

848
00:54:08,779 --> 00:54:12,200
In no part of Oceania do the inhabitants have the feeling that they are a

849
00:54:12,200 --> 00:54:14,860
colonial population ruled from a distant capital.

850
00:54:14,860 --> 00:54:21,137
Oceania has no capital, and its titular head is a person whose whereabouts nobody knows.

851
00:54:21,137 --> 00:54:25,279
Except that English is its chief lingua franca and new speak its official

852
00:54:25,279 --> 00:54:28,520
language, it is not centralized in any way.

853
00:54:28,520 --> 00:54:33,500
Its rulers are not held together by Blood Ties but by adherence to a common doctrine.

854
00:54:33,500 --> 00:54:37,580
It is true that our society is stratified, and very rigidly stratified,

855
00:54:37,580 --> 00:54:41,779
on what at first sight appear to be hereditary lines.

856
00:54:41,779 --> 00:54:45,137
There is far less to and fro movement between the different groups that

857
00:54:45,137 --> 00:54:48,979
happened under capitalism or even in the pre-industrial age

858
00:54:48,979 --> 00:54:52,819
Between the two branches of the Party there is a certain amount of interchange,

859
00:54:52,819 --> 00:54:56,180
but only so much as we'll ensure that weaklings are excluded from the Inner

860
00:54:56,180 --> 00:55:01,718
Party and that ambitious members of the Outer Party are made harmless by allowing them to rise.

861
00:55:01,718 --> 00:55:05,718
Proletarians, in practice, are not allowed to graduate into the Party.

862
00:55:05,718 --> 00:55:10,099
The most gifted among them, who might possibly become nuclei of discontent, are

863
00:55:10,099 --> 00:55:13,400
simply marked done by the Thought Police and eliminated.

864
00:55:13,400 --> 00:55:17,360
But this state of affairs is not necessarily permanent, nor is it a matter

865
00:55:17,360 --> 00:55:21,319
of principle. The Party is not a class in the old sense of the word.

866
00:55:21,319 --> 00:55:25,637
It does not aim at transmitting power to its own children, as such; and if there

867
00:55:25,637 --> 00:55:29,058
were no other way of keeping the ableist people at the top, it would be perfectly

868
00:55:29,058 --> 00:55:33,619
prepared to recruit an entire new generation from the ranks of the proletariat.

869
00:55:33,619 --> 00:55:37,159
In the crucial years, the fact that the Party was not a hereditary body did a

870
00:55:37,159 --> 00:55:39,797
great deal to neutralize opposition.

871
00:55:39,797 --> 00:55:42,979
The older kind of socialists who had been trained to fight against something

872
00:55:42,979 --> 00:55:48,080
called 'class privilege', assumed that what is not hereditary cannot be permanent. He

873
00:55:48,080 --> 00:55:52,159
did not see that the continuity of an oligarchy need not be physical, nor did

874
00:55:52,159 --> 00:55:57,080
he pause to reflect that hereditary aristocracies have always been short-lived whereas adoptive

875
00:55:57,080 --> 00:56:00,319
organizations such as the Catholic Church have sometimes lasted for

876
00:56:00,319 --> 00:56:02,599
hundreds or thousands of years.

877
00:56:02,599 --> 00:56:06,619
The essence of oligarchical rule is not father to son inheritance, but the

878
00:56:06,619 --> 00:56:10,457
persistence of a certain worldview and a certain way of life, imposed by the dead

879
00:56:10,457 --> 00:56:11,900
upon the living.

880
00:56:11,900 --> 00:56:15,797
A ruling group is a ruling group so long as it can nominate its successes

881
00:56:15,797 --> 00:56:21,137
The Party is not concerned with perpetuating its blood but with perpetuating itself.

882
00:56:21,137 --> 00:56:25,099
Who wields power is not important, provided that the hierarchical structure

883
00:56:25,099 --> 00:56:27,680
remains always the same.

884
00:56:27,680 --> 00:56:32,779
All the beliefs, habits, tastes, emotions, mental attitudes that characterize our

885
00:56:32,779 --> 00:56:36,919
time are really designed to sustain the mystique of the Party and prevent the

886
00:56:36,919 --> 00:56:41,419
true nature of present-to-day society from being perceived. Physical rebellion,

887
00:56:41,419 --> 00:56:45,979
or any preliminary move toward rebellion, is at present not possible.

888
00:56:45,979 --> 00:56:50,718
From the proletarians nothing is to be feared. Left to themselves, they will

